WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.377
Now scale the small neural-network idea up to a decoder-only L L M.

00:00:05.377 --> 00:00:10.297
Token I D's first use learned embedding weights to create vectors.

00:00:10.297 --> 00:00:17.972
The model also needs information about token order, because the same words in a different order can mean something

00:00:17.972 --> 00:00:23.787
different. Modern models use positional methods such as rotary position information.

00:00:23.787 --> 00:00:26.394
We do not need the full mathematics here.

00:00:26.844 --> 00:00:30.891
The representations then pass through many Transformer blocks.

00:00:30.891 --> 00:00:36.036
Attention and feed-forward layers repeatedly update the hidden states.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:42.727
The final hidden state is projected through learned output weights to produce vocabulary log its.
